      "text": "The following events are possible:\n\n$6, 6$\n$5, 6$\n$4, 6$\n$3, 6$\n$2, 6$\n$1, 6$\n$6, 5$\n$5, 5$\n$4, 5$\n$3, 5$\n$2, 5$\n$6, 4$\n$5, 4$\n$4, 4$\n$3, 4$\n$2, 4$\n$6, 3$\n$5, 3$\n$4, 3$\n$3, 3$\n$2, 3$\n$6, 2$\n$5, 2$\n$4, 2$\n$3, 2$\n$2, 2$\n\nThis is a total of 24 possible events, and $\\boxed{\\frac{13}{18}}$ of them have primes sums.\n\nTo solve this problem, we need to first determine all possible outcomes when two standard 6-sided dice are tossed. Each die has 6 faces, so there are \\(6 \\times 6 = 36\\) total possible outcomes.\n\nNext, we need to identify which of these outcomes result in a prime number sum. The prime numbers when added together in the range from 2 to 12 are 2, 3, 5, 7, and 11. We will then count how many of these possible outcomes result in these prime sums.\n\nFinally, we will calculate the probability by dividing the number of favorable outcomes by the total number of possible outcomes.",
